    Compute the reduced witness entries from the matrix runs
    
    A table entry is the scalar product of one run of matrix cells with the run's point; the entries follow in row-major then run order. The computation checks the run divides the row, the point length matches the run, and the cell count matches the matrix. Unit tests cover the entry order, the inner product and the named shape rejections.
    
    This is partial progress: the first-chain wiring is the next step.

